From: Leopold Li <leopold.lixiaoliang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:44:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(gateway): queue drain must not drop pending on
 None-prepare
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug
---
When ``_run_agent_inner``'s drain loop dequeued a queued follow-up event
whose ``@`` context reference was blocked,
``_prepare_profile_scoped_inbound_message_text`` returned ``None`` and the
drain loop did ``return result`` — silently abandoning the dequeued event
AND every subsequent message in the queue for that session.

The pattern observed in the wild (WeChat DM, single user):

    10:03:29  inbound  ← "msg1" (queued while agent busy)
    10:03:55  inbound  ← "msg2" (queued)
    10:04:07  "Queued follow-up: final stream delivery not confirmed"
    10:04:17  main-turn response delivered
              → 70s silence, msg1 and msg2 never processed
    10:05:27  inbound  ← "msg3" (overwrites queue slot)

Root cause (gateway/run.py ~line 19913 pre-fix):

    next_message = pending                         # fallback set
    if pending_event is not None:
        ...
        next_message = await self._prepare_profile_scoped_inbound_message_text(...)
        if next_message is None:                   # BUG: silent early return
            return result                          # drops pending_event and queue tail

Fix (Plan B — 3 lines):

    prepared = await self._prepare_profile_scoped_inbound_message_text(...)
    if prepared is not None:
        next_message = prepared
    else:
        logger.debug("Queue drain: prepare returned None; falling back ...")

The raw ``pending`` text set earlier now survives as the fallback and the
drain loop's recursive ``_run_agent`` call always fires.

Upstream status (checked 2026-07-20, v0.18.2)
---------------------------------------------
Not fixed upstream. Nearby but unrelated PRs/commits reviewed:
  * #31496 fix(gateway): third-sender debounce drop — base.py, group chat
  * #61027 fix(gateway): interrupt-depth follow-up — legacy queue_message
  * cd0219d fix(gateway): stop slow restart redelivery loops

None touch _run_agent_inner's drain block.

Tests
-----
Existing regression suite (unchanged behaviour):
  tests/gateway/test_queue_consumption.py           14 tests, all pass
  tests/gateway/test_pending_drain_no_recursion.py   5 tests, all pass

New adapter-surface regression suite:
  tests/gateway/test_queue_drain_ftest.py            3 tests, all pass
    - test_baseline_single_queued_followup_delivered
    - test_multiple_queued_followups_delivered_in_fifo_order
    - test_handler_exception_on_followup_does_not_stick_session

A runner-level unit test that mocks _prepare_ ... -> None inside a real
_run_agent call is deferred (needs a large mock harness for _run_agent_inner's
~30 collaborators). See TODO block at the bottom of test_queue_drain_ftest.py.

Runner script
-------------
scripts/run-queue-ftests.sh drives the three files above as one command
so the suite is easy to run post-upgrade or from a daily Hermes cron.

